+# Fixed Phone Snapshot reuse audit
+
+Source: exact Git object5e8ff8aa19571f5718b982dc47a165b8f22e0dc0. No moving
+Phone worktree, reference edit, compile or device use. Per-file SHA/bytes and
+verbatim original objects are retained in phone-source-provenance.json.
+
+Reusable: native-owned typed originals, expected SHA/restoreId CAS, partial
+restore classification, immutable handback and non-revivable retire. Manager's
+featureCompareRestoreEntries checks typed current scoped raw under its write
+lock, updates that scoped map, then emits queued worker signals AFTER unlock.
+This ordering and responsibility split can inform the later Pico lease.
+
+Not the missing Pico proof: Phone Snapshot::featureSnapshotSettings reads
+_snapshotFormat.isSet/get before capturing raw entries, initializing that
+cache. It does not preserve an originally uninitialized format handle, and its
+14 keys include previousAnimatedSnapUrl but not snapshotAnimatedDuration. Its
+native source does not capture independent Handle default/initialized flags,
+WeakManager or registration mementos. Applying it by rename would weaken Pico.
+
+SettingManager uses a lazy WriteWorker QSettings cache; valueChanged/keyRemoved
+are queued connections. The restore helper verifies Manager memory and format
+cache, but publishes no exact worker-cache, backing-store original or queue
+completion checkpoint. The runtime test checks typed Manager+format memory and
+partial restore, then terminates the worker at final exit; that final shutdown
+is not a pre-restore original backend/cache/queue lease proof.
+
+SNAPSHOT_HANDOFF_AUDIT covers passive measurement histories, actual bounded
+Account owner-thread dispatch, cancelled late callbacks and source retirement.
+Its queue patterns can inform bounded work, but it grants no Settings worker
+restoration authority. No generic claim is made that Phone lacks a complete
+source composition: this audit distinguishes the concrete reusable source from
+the stronger Pico original lazy-state/backend prerequisites now required.
+
+No native backend/restore implementation was changed after this read-only audit.
