+# Private Snapshot NativeLease3 Host checkpoint composition
+
+This proposal is private and unapplied. It depends on the separately frozen,
+uncompiled Native17 packet. It does not restore settings, qualify a Native
+writer/close/backend, or complete the common-v16 Snapshot journey.
+
+## Actual boundary
+
+An exact already prepared Source2 Parent and its exact warm baseline, reader,
+raw owner, lock, configured process and codec remain authoritative. No cold
+adoption, replacement baseline, input authority, new service or extra archive
+is introduced. A Native3 owner attaches before its constructor I/O and retains
+the same Raw owner in existing unresolved custody until a future real Native
+retirement can be proved. Its own original LifecycleProcessFile root is in the
+same Snapshot namespace. Missing both Host root names cannot permit cleanup.
+
+The actual Source2 reader callbacks are reused for command dispatch. Candidate
+admission/Native guard construction is not retrospectively described as raw
+qualified. There is no production Binding factory for this private owner yet.
+The checkpoint component deliberately remains before ordinary input: the Parent
+must still be prepared, with zero deliveries. It is not a normal Close or
+restore integration.
+
+A closed version3 capture or observe command has one original earliest Host/
+Native epoch anchor. The actually later Native TSI request epoch must remain
+inside this unchanged window; response capture is independently checked against
+the current Native epoch. It cannot renew the Host expiry. The issued owner row and complete reservation are durable
+before dispatch. There is no polling/retry after an ignored or unknown result.
+The current response plus two fixed ranges of the actual original file and its
+actual retained pending marker are FOUR physical SDK returns. Each is archived
+through the existing Raw2 chunks/bundles before framing, UTF8, JSON, source age
+or semantic refusal. A current Test.saveObject response does not authorize the
+original checkpoint: the actual original file extent, whole SHA, both range
+stamps, Native proof, root node and actual pending bytes must join independently.
+The typed QDataStream remains opaque; no replacement settings values are sent.
+
+All successful observations still return mutationReady=false,
+writerQualified=false, settingsRestored=false, backendObserved=false and
+workerCacheObserved=false. Both Host close methods deliberately refuse Native3
+custody; there is no Native retirement or restored-settings success API.
+
+## One budget
+
+The original Raw2 wire69632B/canonical98304B/2MiB copy profile is unchanged.
+FOUR complete2MiB workspaces are reserved together, not specialized to observed
+small packets. Native original/intent/pending/current leaves reserve five parts,
+12 descriptor slots and229376B of original/copy/metadata extent in the same
+family. Actual physical Raw parts consume the same512-part ceiling. There is
+no per-reader namespace or new16MiB lane. Root64KiB, query34, checkpoint16,
+1.5s source and earliest Raw120s bounds remain fixed; no continuation can reset
+them. Native3 uses explicit Host root3/command3/framing3; Raw attempt/reference2
+retains its original opaque-byte semantics and Source1/2 remain default.
+
+The declared24-record Host ledger corpus uses existing real writers, bundle
+records and original OFDs. Its valid pre-reservation bill was9829575B. Adding
+all8388608B prospective copies gives18218183B, so admission actually refuses
+against16777216B. The issued row retains admitted=false and the full reservation;
+there are zero new Native3 commands/getters and no replay. These records are
+Host resource input, not measurements of Native events or a restored live owner.
+
+## Evidence and qualification
+
+Each final private scope has a120s process watchdog, actual wait status, two
+kernel-absence observations, exact loaded-source SHA/full8stat before and after,
+and retained original file SHA/full8stat across process exit where inventoried.
+The Source1/2 compatibility37 retains the existing fixtures' cleanup semantics;
+its Native-specific inventory counter is0, not a claim that all default fixture
+originals were retained. Exact earlier epochs remain in their separate receipt
+folders and are not relabeled after the custody/metadata/clock corrections.
+
+Actual Host Python factories, immutable files, CAS/OFD boundaries and binary
+SDK wrapper entry points execute. Native/Qt/Android producer behavior in Host
+composition tests is a declared model. The independent fixed-script tests run
+on real GNU Host files/PID/start/epoch; this is not Android shell, Native C++,
+Qt/QSettings, physical device or backing-store qualification. Native17 remains
+byte-frozen and uncompiled; no repository files or remote state were changed.
+
+The final Host18 scope passed18.780s (18.808s measured including receipt),
+252 loaded source pins unchanged,399 retained files unchanged across exit.
+The final affected7 passed2.858s: four existing Source2 compatibility cases and
+three real GNU Host script cases,244 loaded source pins unchanged,8 actual
+shell files unchanged across exit. Both used their own120s watchdogs, exit0 and
+two kernel-absence observations. HEAD at each start and end was1063409024.
+The earlier defaults37 passed47.607s on its explicitly preserved epoch.
+Native request-clock counters first produced two genuine failures (false refusal
+of a later real request; false acceptance of a future response), then both
+passed1.966s after the narrow original-window correction. The rejected receipts
+and their exact source copies are retained.
+
+Durable repository test afterimages preserve every exercised TestCase body by
+AST equality. Only standard repository import-path setup, license comments and
+placement of the direct __main__ runner at the end are adapted from the private
+imported test files. That packaging delta is not described as a repository
+execution result; Root must run the exact repository selectors after selection.
+
+## Remaining work
+
+Review and select these afterimages before any repository apply. A future
+explicit production factory must retain the same warm carrier before its first
+Native dispatch. Actual Native compilation/runtime, barrier/holder validity,
+configured QSettings backend/worker cache/backing-file/queue proof, durable
+restore-intent/one-shot writes and complete Native retirement remain separate
+unfulfilled prerequisites. Existing NormalClosed failure86.593s at its original
+final1.5s fence remains RED; this component does not qualify it or retry it.
