+# Private Snapshot Host4 Worker metadata join
+
+This is a new private afterimage copy over frozen Host6. Frozen Host6 and
+Worker5 are unchanged. No repository/native/probe/Binding/device/build/remote
+mutation is authorized or claimed by these Host tests.
+
+## One actual owning path
+
+`SnapshotSettingsNativeLease3.create(context, worker_metadata=True)` explicitly
+selects Host layout4. DefaultFalse preserves layout3 and its capture/observe
+command shape. Both use the same existing Source2 warm Parent, Raw2 owner,
+namespace, immutable writer, binary transport and original process/SourceLock.
+No cold/live adoption, fresh baseline or second archive is introduced.
+
+Host4 composes `capture → worker-capture → observe → worker-observe` over Native
+command3 and nested Worker observation1. The actual baseline/Host/fixed-file
+SDK-wrapper Python paths execute with a declared Native/Qt worker producer.
+Each operation retains FOUR actual binary return wires, including the two
+original memento ranges and actual pending marker. All returned bytes are
+archived before framing/UTF8/JSON, source-age or observation acceptance. The
+worker subsource reports metadata only; it grants no typed-cache, parse-effect,
+backing-file, OFD, full-alias, global-queue, restore or mutation qualification.
+
+## Durable lifetime, one budget
+
+Before the first worker dispatch, the SAME original owner durably writes its
+worker-issued marker, full four-return8MiB transport reservation and additive
+196608B Native resident custody. The real complete existing namespace bill and
+original1.5s fence then admit or refuse actual send. The original Raw120s,
+Host16-history/64KiB-root, Native512-command and global512 physical SDK/parts +
+16MiB bounds remain separate and unchanged. There is no worker bank/reset.
+
+Worker lifetime is tied to an independently pinned original issued receipt,
+not just mutable memory flags. That exact receipt is retained before its CAS,
+and its typed disk copy/bytes must remain present. The bill derives the resident
+cost from this unresolved custody. Successful return clears only the transient
+transport reservation. No code clears worker resident custody or treats process
+exit/memory clearing as Native worker/lease retirement. Host close still refuses.
+
+A genuine negative first passed an actual own CAS clearing resident/original
+flags and then erroneously admitted ordinary observe while the declared Native
+worker original still existed. That RED is preserved. The receipt correction
+makes the same counter refuse before a new Native operation, retains the
+original ownership and passes its affected counter. No quota is relaxed.
+
+## Actual resource edge
+
+An explicitly declared Host resource corpus uses existing Raw2 bundle/chunk
+writers, original OFDs and full-byte/stat namespace guards. It is not evidence
+of Native operations or adoption of a historical live owner.22 records contain
+1284952B; the actual pre-issued bill reports92 parts, stored1875334B,
+decoded6071593B and transient2219323B.
+
+The measured prior decoded+transient bill is8290916B. Adding the unchanged full
+8388608B transport profile gives a projected prospective bound16679524B, below
+16777216B. Adding the required196608B worker resident gives16876132B, above it.
+New issued receipt/header/CAS metadata adds further cost. These are arithmetic
+prospective bounds from the actual prior bill, NOT a tested successful branch
+with the worker reservation removed. The actual complete namespace admission
+refuses: worker-issued/admitted=false, full reservation and custody remain,
+with ZERO new Native dispatch, SDK return or declared worker allocation.
+
+## Evidence epochs
+
+The first seven cases passed on the pre-custody draft. Its outer harness wrongly
+compared `stat` to `stat8` dictionaries and labeled169 originals changed; the
+faulty receipt remains preserved. A fresh passive comparison of exactly those
+same169 original files using their original SHA/eight fields found ZERO changes.
+This was a private runner issue, not a product or storage correction.
+
+The first six-method fence group preserved two real fixture-construction errors:
+its second parameterized fixture inherited the first fixture's mocked1970 clock
+and could not create the synthetic ZIP/APK timestamp. Tests were split into
+separate cases, without changing runtime/clocks/limits. The corrected eight
+fences passed14.828s/242 loaded SHA+8stat unchanged/176 originals unchanged.
+
