+# PRIVATE Snapshot NativeLease3 barrier prerequisite
+
+No repository mutation, compiler, generated CMake configuration, Qt/native run,
+device, service, Domain or remote action took place. This packet extends PRIVATE
+Lease3 afterimages only. Both earlier review packets remain byte-frozen.
+
+## Exact scope and actual paths
+
+Seven existing-file afterimages and two new headers are under `proposed/`:
+
+- SettingInterface.h/.cpp: one shared-library context definition and original
+  Interface init/deinit/maybeInit/load/save/isSet access entries.
+- SettingHandle.h: actual get(other), isSet, getDefault, set/remove/deprecate and
+  existing passive Snapshot cache readers. get() delegates to get(other), reset
+  delegates to set; destructor calls deinit. Constructors before registration do
+  not access existing persistent Snapshot caches. Actual persistent duration/
+  format use sites are SnapshotAnimated.cpp96, Snapshot.cpp878/884 and
+  PreferencesDialog.cpp301/330/331. The conservative bool cache still has no
+  actual current native read consumer. No existing persistent handle copy at
+  these source callsites was found; this is not a claim that generated Handle
+  copy/move operations or arbitrary custom subclasses are globally instrumented.
+- SettingManager.h/.cpp: original register/removeHandle, load/saveSetting,
+  setValue/remove/clear, forceSave and termination, plus the actual original
+  WriteWorker init/start/set/remove/clear/sync/finish/terminate/featureChatSnapshot.
+- CreateBrowseSettingOwner.h and AvatarPreferenceSnapshot.h: their existing
+  direct same-worker QSettings reads also announce worker activity. The existing
+  Avatar and Create responsibilities/restore keys are unchanged.
+- New SnapshotSettingsBarrier3.h and the private extended
+  SnapshotSettingsLease3.h. The earlier core header remains unchanged elsewhere.
+
+Pure Manager allKeys/fileName queries hold only the existing Manager read lock
+and never mutate cache/registration rows or dispatch virtual Handle code. They
+need no new mutation gate. Scope2 Manager readers keep their existing source
+format/path; private Handle hooks add only gated bookkeeping. No default input,
+serializer, raw setting key, settings value or initialization call is changed.
+
+## Lock order and scope
+
+The sole barrier is created in the original Manager only in E2E+Pico builds with
+--testScript, and the SAME shared pointer is given to the original WriteWorker
+BEFORE worker thread startup. No Manager is rediscovered from worker callbacks.
+Other builds and ordinary non-testScript construction retain the exact existing
+QSettings allocation path. No activation endpoint has been added.
+
+Actual Snapshot handle entries classify the fourteen root keys, slash aliases
+and descendants. Alias/descendant/empty/oversized keys invalidate the lease while
+the ordinary product call continues. These keys are NOT normalized into adopted
+original rows. Capture refuses existing alias/descendant rows/registrations with
+an explicit bounded namespace precondition (4096 entries per map,1MiB key text).
+Overlarge unrelated keys conservatively refuse rather than create unbounded scan
+work. Raw original names remain unchanged. The slash classification follows the
+existing Pico observer convention and Qt5.15 normalizedKey; full target Qt encoding
+and external writer proof remain unqualified.
+
+All Manager write/registration/virtual-dispatch entries acquire the Snapshot gate
+before the existing Manager lock, even for unrelated keys, only when a lease is
+selected. This conservative scope is necessary because an existing Manager-held
+virtual callback or custom value destructor can enter a Snapshot handle path.
