+# Private Snapshot NativeLease3 memento/intent core
+
+This is an unapplied, uncompiled source proposal. No repository file was edited.
+Source1 and Source2 retain their existing behavior. The private f8758 decoded-group
+packet is separate and unchanged; neither proposal grants the other authority.
+
+## Scope
+
+One new gated `SnapshotSettingsLease3.h`, plus friend-only private afterimages for
+`SettingInterface.h`, `SettingHandle.h` and `SettingManager.h`. Every addition is
+inside `OVERTE_E2E_FEATURE_TESTS && ANDROID_APP_PICO_INTERFACE`; runtime capture
+requires the original GUI thread and `--testScript`. There is no Snapshot callsite,
+TSI endpoint, probe, host reader, restore execution, public capability or retire.
+
+The native caller must supply actual persistent Snapshot format `Handle<QString>`,
+static duration `Handle<float>`, and conservative static animated `Handle<bool>`.
+Their exact keys are checked. The bool memento is an explicit Lease3 field; Source2
+is not reinterpreted. It is not evidence that the current journey consumes that
+static bool cache.
+
+Capture retains exact raw presence/invalid-value distinctions for the fourteen
+Snapshot keys, closed primitive QVariant types, actual cache/default values,
+initialized/set/deprecated flags, weak Manager bindings, and scoped registration
+rows. No get/isSet/maybeInit/remove/deinit is used. Only absent registrations or the
+three original persistent handles are admitted. Foreign/expired nonempty weak
+bindings refuse, rather than collapsing them into an absent binding. The retained
+weak binding remains a weak binding. Explicit native float/double payload bytes
+supplement QDataStream typing, including negative zero and nonfinite payloads;
+this private signature is same-process/ABI only, not a portable persisted format.
+
+The existing actual Manager worker pointer/birth/thread is pinned without reading
+or initializing its QSettings from the GUI thread. Missing/replaced workers refuse.
+Two bounded zero-wait Manager read-lock windows capture and compare. Serialization
+and hashing occur after lock release; no journal, callback, queue wait, sync or
+worker operation occurs under that lock.
+
+`observe()` returns a fresh same-lease current typed digest. A closed restore-intent
+command has exactly schemaVersion=3 (Int), runId, leaseId, restoreId and
+expectedSha256. It cannot supply replacement keys/values/paths. A syntactically
+valid same-lease attempt becomes IntentPending BEFORE the current read. CAS,
+identity or original-clock loss becomes sticky Refused; the original and acquired
+intent responsibility remain in the original object. A copied/new restore ID
+cannot issue a second read or mutation. The original capture Host-independent
+native 120s and each observation/intent's 1.5s are checked without renewal of the
+whole lease. No Host/Parent/action anchor is composed yet, so these checks do not
+qualify the existing journey's whole clocks.
+
+## Explicit missing boundaries
+
+This core DOES NOT restore even Manager memory and always reports
+`writerQualified=false` and `settingsRestored=false`.
+
+The Manager read lock does not by itself cover every original Handle mutation.
+Two equal reads are provisional mementos, not proof of an uninterrupted Snapshot
+mutation barrier. The next implementation must instrument the actual scoped
+Handle/Manager write, registration, clear and termination paths; capture and
+restore must share that one original barrier/sequence. No Avatar barrier authority
+is borrowed.
+
+There is no original backing-file/cache proof, worker-QSettings-null handling,
+worker drain, original physical settings encodings/unowned rows, durable intent
+journal or acknowledgment, pending result retirement, or original live Snapshot
+factory ownership. The object must be strongly retained by that future original
+Snapshot owner before it is exposed. Process death cannot restore from these
+unpersisted native mementos; no cold adoption or retry is supported. No new source
+namespace/budget is granted: actual endpoint integration must reserve all copies,
+metadata and records in the existing Snapshot512/16MiB family before I/O.
+
+No actual C++/Qt/OS execution, JNI/device, GPU, chooser, restore or complete common
+journey is qualified. Existing NormalClose83.255 pre-send1.5s refusal stays RED.
+
+## Checks
+
+`test_lease3_core_contract.py` runs only host Python, six structural checks over
+actual current source/private afterimages and seven explicitly abstract state
+models. The models do not execute the proposed C++ or QVariant serializer. Cases
+cover typed absent/present-invalid/flag differences, floating payloads, foreign
+run/lease/worker/Manager admission, late read, original whole-clock exhaustion,
+unknown/lost intent return and no second attempt. Source checks verify original
+source hashes, friend-only changes, no settings mutations/initializers, exact
+command keys, sticky admission order, bounded lock scope and explicit float bits.
+
+Final result:13 GREEN in0.057s; all13 explicitly selected source SHA+full8stat
+inputs unchanged before/after. No repository import/runtime run is claimed.
+The first structural checker incorrectly matched UUID QString.remove('-') as a
+settings remove; its single test assertion failure is preserved separately. The
+checker now scopes removal to settings handle/Manager calls. A source-only review
+also made conditional template-pointer conversions to Interface explicit. Neither
+was a real native execution result.
+
+## Proposed next step
+
+Review this core before any application. Then extend the SAME native owner with
+a Snapshot-specific mutation admission and a staged native-owned durable intent
+receipt (still before any write). Independently capture existing same-worker
+QSettings and actual backing file before designing the one-shot scoped restore.
+Do not turn this memento/intent core into a success flag or Manager-only restore.
