+# Snapshot QSettings backend: source facts and missing actual authority
+
+This inspection ran no build tool, qmake, target process, SDK, device or QSettings
+constructor. It does not identify an installed Qt library or a live settings file.
+
+The existing interface main first calls setupHifiApplication(BuildInfo::INTERFACE_NAME).
+SharedUtil.cpp sets applicationName, modified organization and organizationDomain
+from BuildInfo; their deployed values are not inferred here. Later main.cpp447
+calls Setting::init. SettingInterface.cpp65 sets the global default to JSON_FORMAT.
+SettingHelpers.cpp registers that custom `.json` format with readJSONFile and
+writeJSONFile, whose values use the actual JSON encoder/decoder, not a proposed
+INI replacement. The old INI migration temporarily changes the default and
+restores JSON_FORMAT before Manager creation. The old `Interface.ini.lock` comment
+is not evidence that the current backend is INI.
+
+Manager constructs the ORIGINAL WriteWorker and starts its thread. The startup
+connection to WriteWorker::start is commented out. Worker::_qSettings starts null
+and Worker::init allocates `new QSettings()` lazily. Separately, Manager's own
+constructor creates a temporary QSettings, records its fileName and loads raw
+rows. Therefore an original null worker cache does NOT imply an absent backing
+file. Manager::_fileName also cannot prove the later actual worker's selected
+format/path if global Qt application/default-format configuration changed.
+
+The Pico Gradle route loads release/source-inputs.groovy, which uses the reviewed
+pico-source-inputs.py resolver. It requires explicit graphRoot, binding SHA and
+source identity; the resolver constrains target and host Qt to the same5.15 recipe.
+The local runtime patch addresses Android startup/JNI/timezone behavior, with no
+QSettings backend hunk found. This source route is not an admitted configured
+package. All four required PICO_SOURCE_GRAPH_ROOT/PICO_SOURCE_INPUTS/
+PICO_SOURCE_INPUTS_SHA256/PICO_EXPECTED_SOURCE_SHA environment bindings are absent
+in this shell. No source graph/package has been adopted or tooling run to create
+one. No Android preferences backend, physical INI path, custom format integer or
+user/organization path is guessed.
+
+Before any settings restore can become ready, the original same-worker producer
+must passively report actual cache presence, QObject/birth/thread, QSettings format,
+fileName, scope/organization/application/fallback/status and actual registered
+backend/encoding authority. A null cache must remain null; it must not call init,
+sync or construct another QSettings reader. A nonnull cache can require an actual
+matching JSON backend as a narrow prerequisite; support for original null cache
+handback remains missing. Worker data and an independently observed original
+physical file/rows must be joined with original queue/auto-update retirement.
+The Snapshot gate/Manager lock cannot span that worker wait.
+
+The private NativeLease3 file profile preserves opaque ORIGINAL memento/intent
+bytes in the existing private result root. Those files are NOT the product
+settings backend and prove neither its existence nor its restoration. Every
+endpoint result has backendObserved=false,workerCacheObserved=false,
+writerQualified=false,mutationReady=false,settingsRestored=false. No captured
+format/duration baseline is preinitialized to make this prerequisite pass.
