+# PRIVATE NativeLease3 checkpoint and fixed endpoint afterimages
+
+This is unapplied/uncompiled source, not a working native qualification. The
+previous core/barrier/holder packets are unchanged. Actual Host66 group/default
+proof and the later NormalClosed84.624 PRE-SEND1.5s failure remain separate facts.
+
+## Direct vertical
+
+The existing strong native Snapshot owner now holds original and intent bytes
+BEFORE resource open. After the actual existing-handle capture, it exports only
+its retained typed memento bytes (no fresh get/init or Host replacement values),
+adds actual existing Snapshot birth and owner identity, and serializes a bounded
+record. The original manager instance and mutation sequence are inside that record.
+Native references remain held by the original owner; the file is no cold-recovery
+or pointer-registration authority. No original Handle/Manager replacement exists.
+
+The owner persists the original memento before any further current observation.
+It persists the same one-shot core-issued intent before reporting its checkpoint.
+No restore operation exists. After actual acquisition, a separate RESOURCE-only
+permit can finish retaining those bytes even if business time/actor identity was
+lost. It checks original application/process/thread; it never reads source state,
+renews clocks or permits input. Unknown/partial operations retain all bytes and
+original file/directory/pending OFDs. No reopen/resend/adoption follows failure.
+
+A current command rechecks original checkpoint bytes/stamps/OFDs BEFORE the next
+core read. The same pre-dispatch Request3 time anchors and native object-pair pins
+cross both existing AudioSettingsQueue channels. Snapshot AND Manager bindings
+are sealed before client dispatch; replacement during the queue cannot become a
+new captured Manager just because the Snapshot QObject stayed the same. That
+additional queue-pair boundary was not qualified by the earlier frozen holder
+source checks. No earlier receipt is relabeled.
+
+## Existing writer, explicit one-shot profile
+
+The implementation reuses PicoEmoteCaptureFile's EXISTING create/marker/write/
+fsync/readback algorithm, original PicoStreamDescriptor, directory checks and
+strict actual Linux OFD query. No new writer/syscall write loop was introduced.
+Only explicit openSnapshotLease3 selects two fixed leaves:
+
+- feature-pico-snapshot-lease-original.json:98304 actual serialized bytes;
+- feature-pico-snapshot-lease-intent.json:8192 bytes.
+
+Each has a distinct fixed `.pending` leaf. Limits are for these new Native3 roles,
+not an increase to Source1/2 semantic caps or a second512/16MiB budget. The ordinary
+Emote/default open path keeps its original limits and marker. These native roles
+still require actual Host family admission/reservations, which are NOT wired.
+
+The source audit found PicoStreamDescriptor::close ignores both close syscall
+returns before clearing its numeric fields. This is a SOURCE omission, not a
+reproduced native failure. Snapshot3 does NOT execute or claim that close path.
+After complete original file+directory fsync/full readback, the one-shot profile
+retains the exact marker and descriptor OPEN, keeps writing=true and returns only
+a checkpoint proof. Current proof checks actual expected full bytes, named/held
+full stamps, original OFDs/root and retained marker. Further publish/ordinary
+close refuses; there is no unlink or retirement. Any failed proof is sticky.
+This is durable-byte checkpoint DESIGN, not native close/handback or leak-free
+cleanup. Kernel F_DUPFD_QUERY support is still required at runtime; no inode,
+seek or flag fallback is added and no Android kernel support is assumed.
+
+originalDurable/intentDurable in the proposed endpoint mean only those retained
+byte checkpoints; mutationReady,backendObserved,workerCacheObserved,
+writerQualified,settingsRestored are FALSE. Physical product settings/queue proof
+is missing regardless of successful checkpoint writes.
+
+## Fixed endpoint/private dispatcher
+
+Additive TSI public/private afterimages share the SAME original Request3 through
+existing dispatch/client channels, use actual FeatureLifecycle/HMD/private-root
+admission, bind actual TSI birth/canonical result directory and native Snapshot/
+Manager refs once, and keep original1.5/120 fences. They do not change Source1/2.
+The original Snapshot method still passes actual format/duration/bool handles.
+Probe has one closed schema3 action with only capture/observe/restore-intent and a
+once-per-delivery latch before Native/save. Android's existing fixed command route
+reaches this branch. It publishes ONLY feature-pico-snapshot-settings-lease.json
+through the existing Test.saveObject feature path; it creates no new writer.
+
+Test.saveObject still returns void. That CURRENT response file's publication is
+not an original OFD/durable success proof. Missing/throwing/mismatched Native or
+unknown save stays unavailable and is not replayed. The future warm Host Source3
+carrier, fixed raw binary reader, all acquired-byte-before-parse retention,
+original capacity marker and early generic-cleanup refusal are still absent.
+This private native route must not be enabled as mutation-ready or usable Host
+baseline until those joins exist. Current generic cleanup does not know these new
+native pending leaves; Native capture must not precede the future original Host
