+# PRIVATE NativeLease3 original owner and endpoint boundary
+
+No repository source is changed by this proposal. The already reviewed core and
+barrier packets remain immutable; this directory contains new afterimages based
+on them. The six separately approved Host grouped-decode files are installed and
+qualified66 in their explicit scope, not part of this native proposal.
+
+## Actual native source vertical
+
+`proposed/interface/src/ui/Snapshot.cpp` adds a non-invokable private feature
+method on the ACTUAL Snapshot. It passes `_snapshotFormat` and the original static
+`SnapshotAnimated::snapshotAnimatedDuration` and `alsoTakeAnimatedSnapshot`
+references into the SAME native core. No replacement Handle, new registration,
+Settings get/isSet/init/sync or Host value is constructed to establish originals.
+
+`SnapshotSettingsLeaseOwner3` holds actual QSharedPointer<Snapshot> and original
+QSharedPointer<Setting::Manager> plus the core, original request, native run/lease
+identity and command history. It is attached to one out-of-line process slot in
+Snapshot.cpp BEFORE callback connection or the first core read. Snapshot does not
+hold that owner, so there is no owner/Snapshot self-cycle. The unresolved slot is
+intentionally not destroyed at static shutdown. This retains pending original
+responsibility; it is NOT successful cleanup, leak-free retirement or settings
+restore. There is no retire API yet. Only capture may create the first slot;
+observe/intent without that original refuse. Foreign run/TSI/birth/lease cannot
+replace or adopt it. A same-run repeated capture also refuses without recapture.
+
+Existing DependencyManager::get uses a per-thread weak cache. Strong ownership
+would keep an old cached object alive after registry replacement. Consequently,
+this owner has a narrowly gated read-only friend in DependencyManager.h: it reads
+both actual registry entries under the existing registry mutex and rechecks
+inheritance hashes afterward, with dynamic type checks. It never calls get/set,
+constructs a dependency, or changes registry entries. No registry lock overlaps a
+Snapshot gate/Manager lock, callback or wait. Replacements cannot be accepted just
+because a cached old object is still alive. Simultaneous replacement between
+entry/exit observations is still not atomic restore admission; no writes exist.
+
+The extended private core accepts the native owner's actual Manager reference.
+It does not rediscover it through the weak cache. Authoritative current registry
+checks bracket the native operation in the owner. Core retained-context checks
+use the same original worker pointer/birth, the actual original Manager worker
+thread and isRunning, with zero-time Manager read windows outside Snapshot gates.
+The persistent format handle is kept alive by Snapshot ownership; original static
+handles rely on the still-loaded interface module, and all endpoints fail on
+application termination. A real module-unload/lifetime qualification is absent.
+
+Actual Snapshot/Manager/TSI destruction, Manager terminationRequested and
+QCoreApplication::aboutToQuit set a sticky atomic owner failure. The original
+Barrier3 already invalidates before Manager's blocking worker termination; that
+signal callback is additional post-termination refusal, not permission to keep a
+terminated writer valid. Failed/unknown/late responses retain both strong originals
+and any core mementos/issued intent. No automatic destruction, cold adoption,
+resend or clock renewal occurs. Direct foreign raw QObject deletion remains an
+unqualified Qt ownership violation; these source checks do not execute Qt.
+
+## Closed operation schema and original clocks
+
+The sole command action is `feature-pico-snapshot-settings-lease`, schema3 with
+exact fields:
+
+`schemaVersion,action,commandId,runId,operation,leaseId,restoreId,expectedSha256`.
+
+Only actual Int/Double exactly3 is admitted at this native JSON boundary (bool and
+other types refuse). All other fields are exact QString. commandId/runId/birth
+are32 lowercase hex. Capture requires empty lease/restore/SHA. Observe requires
+an actual native-issued lease and empty restore/SHA. Restore-intent requires the
+same lease, one restoreId and64-hex expected-current SHA. No replacement key,
+setting value, output path or permission flag is accepted. Native command typed
+bytes are pinned once at original TSI binding and checked before each core call
+and final return; changing a number's QVariant type is a change too.
+
+Only capture, observe and restore-intent exist. Intent is reserved once in the
+same original core BEFORE any later durability result. It always reports
+intentDurable=false,writerQualified=false,settingsRestored=false. There is NO
+restore mutation, intent acknowledgment, retirement or Manager-only handback API.
+The512 native command ceiling is not a second Host lane or a renewal of the shared
+Snapshot family limit. Future Host family accounting must charge all native
+request/response/memento/file metadata before execution; it is not wired here.
+
+Request3 starts its actual elapsed/epoch anchor BEFORE copying the native command
+and BEFORE either existing dispatch/client queue. Binding TSI context is once-only
+and pins original typed bytes. The same shared request crosses both queues; it
+must not be reconstructed by recursive public TSI invocation. Owner120 starts
