+# Private NativeLease3 Worker metadata observation
+
+This is an unapplied source prerequisite, not C++/Qt/runtime, cache, backing-file,
+OFD or full Snapshot qualification. Frozen Native17 and Host6 remain unchanged.
+No repository files, device, compiler, service, Domain or remote state were used.
+
+## Concrete integration
+
+Two explicit operations, `worker-capture` and `worker-observe`, extend the
+existing closed NativeLease3 command shape without adding replacement values.
+Only those operations return a nested `snapshotWorkerObservationVersion:1`.
+Existing Native capture/observe/original-memento/read/default bodies remain
+unchanged. Source1/2 and frozen Host6 are not upgraded or adopted.
+
+The same existing Native holder retains Snapshot and Manager strong identities.
+The original Worker and optional QSettings objects retain their genuine QObject
+identity/lifetime checks through QPointer; no owning shared pointer is invented
+for worker/cache objects managed by Qt. A separate original-presence bit prevents
+a dead originally present cache from becoming a false absent original.
+
+Core captures its existing original Manager/Handle memento, releases its gate
+and Manager locks, reads only original binding metadata under a bounded Manager
+lock, releases that lock, then uses the existing AudioSettingsQueue client
+channel. No Manager/barrier window spans a queued wait. The exact original
+Request1.5s and earliest Native lease120s timers are checked before/after the
+actual worker metadata callback. Queue cancellation and incomplete results are
+sticky; original/current/pending packets and actual queued functor ownership
+remain retained. A post-queue original Core memento and mutation sequence must
+still match before the metadata is published. A new original worker capture
+also requires that memento match the original Native lease capture.
+
+The queued callback observes the original worker `_qSettings` pointer on its
+actual thread. Null remains null. On an existing object it reads only fileName,
+format and status. It never calls contains/value/allKeys, initializes or creates
+QSettings/Handles, synchronizes, emits a settings signal, writes a key/file or
+reads a physical file. Neither pointer presence nor these source tests prove
+materialized typed cache, getter allocator behavior, full alias inventory,
+backing-file custody or global FIFO emptiness. All corresponding flags remain
+false. Metadata paths stay Native-owned; output contains explicit UTF8 name
+hashes, not private filenames.
+
+The original metadata is Native-owned memory, not durable backend originals.
+`originalDurable`, `mutationReady`, `writerQualified` and `settingsRestored`
+remain false in the nested observation. The outer Native3 originalDurable flag
+continues to describe only its earlier Snapshot memento checkpoint. It must
+never be interpreted as worker/backing-store durability.
+
+## Budget boundary
+
+The producer declares an additive `HostAdditionalResidentBytes=196608` for three
+bounded64KiB metadata packets and retains that local slice after failure.
+Preflight occurs before helper/job allocation. Internal paths are bounded4096
+characters before UTF8/hash encoding, compact metadata8192B and typed metadata
+65536B. This bounds the retained proposed protocol profile; it is not a whole
+Qt allocator/RSS proof. Qt metadata getter internal allocations remain
+unexecuted/unqualified.
+
+The Native local reservation is NOT a second16MiB allowance and does not prove
+the Host global bill. Frozen Host6 intentionally rejects both worker operations.
+A future explicit carrier must add this resident delta to the SAME original
+512-part/16MiB/64KiB-root family BEFORE dispatch, with its existing original
+anchors, all actual return accounting and full physical guards. No present
+production family admission or usable worker endpoint is claimed from this
+private packet. A possible1MiB backend cannot be replaced by the98KiB original
+memento or by metadata hashes.
+
+## Evidence
+
+22 checks passed:8 C++ source contracts,11 declared Native/Qt threaded Python
+models and3 actual private JS dispatcher cases. No native compiler was invoked.
+The declared models exercise actual Python locks, task-owned threads, queue
+ordering and cancellation, including cache-null/dead-cache distinction,
+foreign worker birth/registry, expired request/whole lease, pending callback,
+release of Manager/gate locks during the wait, unchanged command512 and modeled
+additive family admission refusal before packet/getter allocation. This is not
+execution of the proposed C++/Qt algorithm.
+
+The actual private JS branch preserves the same closed command and fixed result
+file, refuses replacement values/missing lease/unknown operations and prevents
+Native replay after lost current-file save. Its Native callee is an explicit
+model. Test.saveObject remains current response publication only.
+
+The owning child used an original120s watchdog, exited0, and was observed absent
+from the kernel twice. All37 explicit private Native17/Host6/new source SHA and
+full8stat pins were unchanged. The first private runner failed before launching
+tests because Native17's manifest is a list while Host6's is a map; that launch
+error is retained separately. No source/test failure or Native result is hidden.
+
+## Remaining prerequisite
+
+Review this five-afterimage source packet before any apply. A real shared-family
+Host carrier, actual Qt/C++ execution, typed-cache/alias observation with proved
+internal read bounds, original backing-file/OFD/queue durability, restore intent,
+exact mutation and retirement are still missing. No normal Snapshot Close or
+full common-v16 journey success is inferred; the preserved86.593s final-fence
+failure stays RED.
