+# Private Snapshot Source2 numerical-cost proposal
+
+No repository source was changed. The candidate is exclusively the explicit Source2 namespace; it grants no Lifecycle, source, input, restoration or current-verdict authority.
+
+## Actual historical method result
+
+The unchanged Closed82 corpus has 412 files, 400 packed values, 1,474,016 stored bytes. Three alternating comparisons preserve 412 fresh full-byte/OFD/8-stat windows and 411 strict canonical-JSON parses per pass. Expanded numerical contributions remain 4,469,700 bytes with a 37,578-byte largest expansion.
+
+Median old 732.185 ms; warm candidate 37.725 ms. Cold candidate 764.867 ms is slower than the original. Warm hits omit 400 repeated unpack/length allocations and their 800 codec full-file guard calls; original outer codec guards remain before and after. All 169 loaded Python source hashes/stamps and all actual corpus hashes/stamps remain unchanged. This is an inner-method result, not complete Namespace.measure/whole-run saving or proof of the first Closed82 exception.
+
+The benchmark excludes warm known-owner traversal, retained current graphs, actual root CAS, endpoint access, full namespace admission, and the exact Closed82 failure cause. Its private fixture guard counters are eight passing helper/real-file cases; they do not qualify actual production namespace composition yet.
+
+## Proposed bounded semantics
+
+Each immutable admitted tuple is (exact ASCII entry name, SHA256 of freshly verified complete bytes, byte extent, expanded contribution, largest expansion). No parsed DTO is retained. Every current pass still performs original named inventory, typed warm-owner scope/manifest guards, current graph sizing, full file bytes/OFD/8-stat, strict JSON, closed chunk version, and final namespace/bookends. Current global totals and quota checks are recomputed. A hit adds the FULL original numerical cost to the SAME actual current bill.
+
+Reserve 4096 fixed metadata bytes plus 768 bytes before each next entry allocation. Name<=128 ASCII, SHA64, extent<=65536, contribution/peak<=16MiB make the canonical entry<=256 bytes; finish checks this actual bound. Three entry copies are covered by768. This is protocol/copy accounting, not a Python RSS bound. Current actual corpus adds319,744 bytes. At most512 immutable entries; saturation takes the original unpack path without replacing/resetting old entries. Partial failed expansion remains pending and cannot provide a hit. Namespace's existing sticky poison path prevents reuse after any failure.
+
+The exact currently used strict/parser/decoder/size entrypoints and their code identities/constants are pinned; codec profile checks remain fresh before/after each full measure, and misses retain original per-unpack before/after checks. Existing Source1 behavior and all original 512/16MiB/64KiB/1.5s/120s bounds remain unchanged.
+
+## Proposed actual integration qualification after review
+
+Use the existing Source2 fixture and same one actual typed warm namespace, never adopt the historical corpus as a live owner. Compare cold/warm full returned bill with expected added metadata and count actual fresh windows. Add current byte/8-stat mutation, equal foreign function, code/constant/row alias replacement, full512 fallback, exact metadata-capacity refusal before getter, and interrupted-miss poison/retained raw ownership. Run affected existing16. Only then consider one changed normal Close flow with diagnostic exception-chain recording at the actual final query boundary, keeping the original120 and1.5 seconds. No unchanged whole retry.
+
